# PART 3 — AUTHORIZATION ARCHITECTURE

## 3.1 Authorization Hierarchy

Implement the following logical hierarchy:

```text
GeFlow Platform
    |
    |-- Organization
           |
           |-- Organization Membership
           |       |
           |       |-- Organization Role
           |       |-- Organization Permissions
           |
           |-- Business
           |       |
           |       |-- Business Category
           |       |       |
           |       |       |-- Primary AI Agent
           |       |       |-- Category Permissions
           |       |       |-- Category Resources
           |       |
           |       |-- Branches (if supported)
           |       |
           |       |-- Business Resources
           |
           |-- Authorized Users
           |
           |-- Authorized AI Agents
```

This hierarchy is a logical authorization model. Map it to the actual GeFlow database structure.

Do not assume that an organization and a business are separate database entities. If the current application treats them as the same entity, preserve that model and document the implementation decision.

## 3.2 Mandatory Authorization Decision

A request must be allowed only when all applicable checks pass:

1. User is authenticated.
2. User has access to the requested organization.
3. User has access to the requested business.
4. User has permission for the requested operation.
5. Requested category is valid for the business.
6. User or agent has the required category access.
7. Resource belongs to the authorized organization/business.
8. Any additional existing security policy is satisfied.

A successful organization membership check must not automatically grant unrestricted access to every category.

Similarly, category permission must not grant access to another organization.

