# PART 5 — CATEGORY-LEVEL AUTHORIZATION

## 5.1 Category Access Definition

Category-level authorization controls access to the category-specific capabilities and resources associated with a business.

Use the finalized 29-category registry from Step 05.

The system must resolve category access using verified business-category associations.

Do not trust a category ID supplied directly by a browser without validating it against the actual business record.

## 5.2 Category Permission Structure

Define permissions using a structured naming system.

Examples:

**General category permissions**
- category.read
- category.access
- category.settings.read
- category.settings.manage
- category.reports.read

**Category-specific permissions**
- category.inventory.read
- category.inventory.manage
- category.sales.read
- category.sales.manage
- category.purchases.read
- category.purchases.manage
- category.suppliers.read
- category.suppliers.manage
- category.customers.read
- category.customers.manage

These are permission examples, not permission grants.

The actual permissions must match existing GeFlow modules and authorized workflows.

