## 5.4 Category Access Rules

Implement the following behavior:

1. A business must have a valid category association.
2. Category access must be validated against the business record.
3. An organization member must not automatically receive every category-specific permission.
4. A user must have the required category permission to access restricted category resources.
5. An agent must have an approved mapping to the business category.
6. An agent must not access resources outside its authorized category scope.
7. Category-specific restrictions must be enforced server-side.
8. Invalid or inactive mappings must fail closed.

## 5.5 Multiple Businesses and Categories

If an organization owns multiple businesses with different categories, authorization must be evaluated at the correct business scope.

Example:

```text
Organization A
    |
    |-- Business A1
    |      Category: Pharmacy
    |      Primary Agent: AGT-029
    |
    |-- Business A2
    |      Category: Grocery
    |      Primary Agent: AGT-027
    |
    |-- Business A3
           Category: Fashion
           Primary Agent: AGT-023
```

A user may have access to all three businesses, or only selected businesses, depending on assigned permissions.

Access to the pharmacy business must not automatically grant access to the grocery or fashion business if the user lacks permission for those businesses.

Do not assume that multiple businesses per organization are already supported. Verify the existing data model first.

