# PART 6 — ORGANIZATION + CATEGORY AUTHORIZATION DECISION

## 6.1 Combined Authorization

The final authorization decision must combine:

- Authentication.
- Organization membership.
- Business access.
- Organization permissions.
- Category access.
- Category permissions.
- Resource ownership.
- Existing application policies.

Conceptual logic:

```text
ALLOW REQUEST IF:

Authenticated User
    AND Active Organization Membership
    AND Authorized Business Access
    AND Required Organization Permission
    AND Valid Business Category
    AND Required Category Permission
    AND Valid Resource Ownership
    AND Existing Security Policies Pass

OTHERWISE:

DENY REQUEST
```

This logic must be implemented using the actual backend authorization architecture.

## 6.2 Fail-Closed Behavior

If the system cannot verify:

- Organization membership.
- Business ownership.
- Category mapping.
- User permission.
- Agent authorization.
- Resource ownership.

Then the request must be denied.

Never grant access because of a missing authorization record or failed permission lookup.

