# PART 11 — TESTING REQUIREMENTS

All tests must run in an isolated development or test environment. Do not use production business records for destructive testing.

## 11.1 Organization-Level Tests

- Owner accesses own organization.
- Admin accesses permitted resources.
- Manager accesses assigned resources.
- Member accesses assigned resources.
- Pending member is denied normal access.
- Suspended member is denied access.
- Revoked member is denied access.
- User from Organization A cannot access Organization B.
- User cannot modify another organization's records.
- URL ID manipulation does not bypass access controls.

## 11.2 Category-Level Tests

- User with authorized category permission can access the permitted resource.
- User without category permission is denied.
- Invalid category mapping is denied.
- Inactive category mapping is denied.
- Category ID manipulation is denied.
- Category-specific tools enforce their own permissions.
- Category access does not grant unrelated business access.

## 11.3 Combined Tests

- Organization authorized + category authorized = allowed, subject to all other policies.
- Organization authorized + category unauthorized = denied.
- Organization unauthorized + category authorized = denied.
- Business unauthorized + category authorized = denied.
- Invalid agent mapping = denied.
- Agent unauthorized for category = denied.

## 11.4 AI Agent Tests

- Correct primary agent resolves.
- Wrong agent is rejected.
- Suspended agent is rejected.
- Unauthorized tool call is rejected.
- Agent cannot access another tenant.
- Agent cannot access another business without authorization.
- Agent cannot modify data without required write permission.
- Required approval is enforced.
- Tool execution result is correctly audited.

## 11.5 Regression Tests

Verify that existing GeFlow functions remain operational for authorized users:

- Authentication.
- Dashboard access.
- Business management.
- Products.
- Inventory.
- Purchasing.
- Suppliers.
- Customers.
- POS.
- Reports.
- Existing AI features.
- Existing notifications and other modules identified during inspection.

Do not treat a blocked unauthorized request as a regression.

