- Map organization membership.
- Map business access.
- Map category permissions.
- Map existing roles.
- Identify policy conflicts.
- Identify required changes.

**Gate:** Preserve existing valid authorization behavior.

### Phase 3 — Organization-Level Authorization

Implement only the required organization membership and access enforcement using existing architecture.

### Phase 4 — Category-Level Authorization

Implement category-specific access checks and enforce the approved category mapping.

### Phase 5 — Agent Authorization Integration

Implement the authorization checks needed to ensure the 29-agent architecture cannot bypass organization or category boundaries.

Do not deploy or create the agents.

### Phase 6 — Backend and Database Enforcement

Apply required security controls to affected APIs and data-access paths.

### Phase 7 — Minimal Frontend Integration

Reflect authorized and denied access in existing UI without redesigning unrelated screens.

### Phase 8 — Security and Regression Testing

Run the full required test matrix.

### Phase 9 — Documentation and Completion

Document actual changes, test evidence, unresolved risks and remaining dependencies.

Stop after this phase.

